# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for known-benign, third-party first-use races.
#
# RocksDB caches CPU CRC32C support lazily on the first crc32c() call. The
# first concurrent call races to set an idempotent, read-only flag (every
# thread computes the same value; it is read-only afterward). This is in
# RocksDB's internal util/crc32c.cc, not our code, and there is no clean
# single-threaded trigger to warm it (the header is not public). Benign.
race:IsFastCrc32Supported
race:crc32c.cc

# Note: zlib-ng's analogous lazy functable init race is NOT suppressed here -
# it is eliminated by warming zlib single-threaded in Executor::start().
